# A sibling nested method of a factory reads the host's formal through `node`;
# the returned method calls it. The copied context C is the node of every
# copied nested definition of the host, so the sibling reads the formal's
# staged value (7) and the copied seed (1); the outer seed stays 9.
int: seed 1
fn: readSeed () int
    return: node\seed
end: readSeed
fn: makeOuter (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: helper () int
        return: node\n + readSeed()
    fn: inner () int
        return: helper()
    return: inner
@: held makeOuter(7)
seed: 9
int: got held()
int: ok 7
if: got != 8 || seed != 9
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
